<p>Why this page exists, in the project's own words: a signature on a tower this tall can only be a review or a rubber stamp, and the difference between them is the whole of whether the panel/author separation the method is built on still holds. Stating the tower plainly is the least the record can do for a reader who did not build it. The next author act on the docket is that stamp review — not a fourth delegation.</p>

